* Opener's rebids

Booklet section "SUBSEQUENT BIDDING BY RESPONDER" and the rebid-strength framework
under "RESPONSES AND LATER BIDDING AFTER A 1H OR A 1S OPENING": a minimum opener
(13--15) rebids notrump at the lowest level, raises responder's suit at the
lowest level, or bids a new suit without reversing; a medium opener (16--18)
jump-raises, jump-rebids its own suit, or reverses (there is no reverse available
in the 1!h-1!s auction itself, since spades already belongs to responder); a
maximum opener (19--21) jumps in notrump, double-jumps, or jump-shifts. A new
suit by responder after a one-level response is forcing one round; the fourth
suit is artificial and forcing; a new suit after a 1NT rebid is non-forcing
(a reverse or jump shift there is a game force); a jump preference to the three
level after a two-over-one response is game forcing, and a plain 2-level new-suit
response promises another bid unless opener's rebid is already at game.

** After 1!h-1!s

1H-1S-
1N = 12--14 hcp, bal
2H = 12--15 hcp, 5+!h
2S = 12--15 hcp, 3+!s
2C = 13--18 hcp, 4+!c
2D = 13--18 hcp, 4+!d
2N = 18--19 hcp, bal
3H = 16--18 hcp, 6+!h
3S = 16--18 hcp, 4+!s
3C = 19--21 hcp, 5+!c
3D = 19--21 hcp, 5+!d

1H-1S-2C-
P = 6--9 hcp, not 3+!h, not 5+!s
2D = {prio:-1} F
2H = 6--9 hcp, 3+!h
2S = 6--9 hcp, 5+!s
2N = 10--11 hcp, not 3+!h, not 5+!s
3H = 10--11 hcp, 3+!h
3S = 10--11 hcp, 5+!s

1H-1S-1N-
2C = NF, 5+!c, not 13+ hcp
2D = NF, 5+!d, not 13+ hcp
3C = F, 13+ hcp, 5+!c
3D = F, 13+ hcp, 5+!d

** After 1!s-2!c

1S-2C-
2D = 13--18 hcp, 4+!d
2H = 13--18 hcp, 4+!h
2N = 18--19 hcp, bal
2S = 12--15 hcp, 6+!s
3C = 12--15 hcp, 3+!c
3S = 16--18 hcp, 6+!s

1S-2C-2H-
2N = 10--11 hcp, not 3+!c, not 3+!h
3C = 10--11 hcp, 3+!c
3H = 10--11 hcp, 3+!h
2S = 11--12 hcp, 2=!s
3D = F
3S = {prio:-1} F

** After a minor-suit response to a minor opening

1C-1D-
1H = 13--18 hcp, 4+!h
1S = 13--18 hcp, 4+!s
1N = 12--14 hcp, bal
2C = 12--15 hcp, 5+!c
2D = 12--15 hcp, 4+!d
2N = 18--19 hcp, bal
3C = 16--18 hcp, 6+!c
3D = 16--18 hcp, 4+!d

** After a major-suit response to a minor opening

1C-1H-
1S = 13--18 hcp, 4+!s
1N = 12--14 hcp, bal
2C = 12--15 hcp, 5+!c
2D = 13--18 hcp, 4+!d
2H = 12--15 hcp, 3+!h
2N = 18--19 hcp, bal
3C = 16--18 hcp, 6+!c
3H = 16--18 hcp, 4+!h

A reverse or a jump shift after opener's 1NT rebid is a game force (the
booklet's own example is 1!c-1!h-1NT-2!s or 3!d).

1C-1H-1N-
2S = F, 4+!s
3D = F, 4+!d

1D-1H-
1S = 13--18 hcp, 4+!s
1N = 12--14 hcp, bal
2D = 12--15 hcp, 5+!d
2H = 12--15 hcp, 3+!h
2N = 18--19 hcp, bal
3D = 16--18 hcp, 6+!d
3H = 16--18 hcp, 4+!h
